  "question": {
    "text": "<p>During an experiment with a metre bridge, the galvanometer shows a null point when the jockey is pressed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm </mi></math>using a standard resistance of <math><mn>90</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> ,as shown in the figure. The least count of the scale used in the metre bridge is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi>mm</mi></math>. The unknown resistance is<br ><br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image9-b3319f15-d980-4e53-940f-9365525b918d.png\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
